  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A)=4.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{11x-12}{x+4} \\\\ 4(x+4) & =11x-12 \\\\ 4x+16 & =11x-12 \\\\ 7x & =28 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =11x-12=11(4)-12=32, \\\\ AC & =x+4=4+4=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
